  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T)=3$\n\nII. If $v=[1,0,0]^{T}$ is a solution of $T(x)=0$ then $T$ is invertible.\n\nIII. If there is not $u\\in {R}^{3}$ such that $T(u)=[1,0,0]^{T},$ then $\\text{rank}(T)=3.$",
